            "sourceContextAndLimits": "HB p36 requires the simple orbital model in LK; p37 makes aromatic4.3 compulsory in LK. SH pp50/69/70 separates common resonance from LK wave-mechanical orbital detail; aromatic compounds are LK-compulsory independently of conditional dyes. SN physical57/printed45 LK12LB2 explicitly contains orbital aromatic bonding and resonance energy, with LK11 orbital foundations physical49/printed37. The full supplied energetic152-kJ/mol comparison and interrupted-diene transfer are own operational examples, not claims that every source prescribes these exact numbers or the whole current case.",
